  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is RNA-only multiprofile with PCA and avgpool, which achieved the best accuracy (0.5907) and F1 (0.5727), while single-profile PCA and transformer aggregation were weaker and image-only ResNet was poor. This experiment tests whether replacing PCA with the scgpt RNA encoder improves that same promising multiprofile avgpool setting, cleanly isolating the effect of RNA representation. It is the best next step because it exploits the current best direction with a focused comparison and will clarify whether stronger RNA encoders or multimodal fusion should be prioritized in the remaining budget."
}

